  "sourceUse": "TLS programme Appendix 1 Articles 7 and 8 explicitly govern September 2026 entrants. Art. 8a applies to earlier entrants. The current catalogue repeats semester or year units across blocks and uses older course shells in years two and three. Its empty year-two slot is resolved by 660441-B-6 in Art. 8. Its 6 EC placement and Governance and the Rule of Law reflect older content. Art. 8 specifies the 12 EC placement and The World’s Legal Systems. The separate placement guidance expressly confirms the new 12 EC structure and 90 EC threshold.",
  "progression": {
    "yearOne": "60 EC of introductory public administration, sociology, law, politics, policy, history and methods. Public Administration Research 1 is 9 EC, and the history unit is 3 EC. Orientation and Dutch diagnostic carry zero credits.",
    "yearTwo": "Ten compulsory units worth 60 EC include 6 EC of Public Administration Research 2, public management, governance, finance, legal protection and institutional analysis. Research 2 is explicitly required by the adopted cohort table even though the guide has a blank. A separately dated individual entry is not yet published.",
    "yearThree": "Art. 8 assigns 12 EC to the placement, 12 to the thesis, 18 to minor space and 18 to three compulsory units: Policy Analysis, Supervision, Performance and Accountability, and The World’s Legal Systems. The exact 12 EC placement guidance requires 90 EC before starting and at least 40 working days. The older route’s threshold under Art. 6(2) expressly cross-references Art. 8a and is not used. The thesis regulation and Art. 6(1) require 102 EC after block 1 grades, with a proposal in block 2 and a second-semester desk study. A standard entrant can meet both gates with 120 EC by the end of year two. Minor choices at overseas universities require Examination Board approval."
  }
}
